.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::NodeCenteredFiniteVolumeTransport\fP< dim >::TransformScalarBoundaryValuesIntoNeumannConditions (\fBBOX_BOUNDARY\fP boundary, const char * node_property, const char * propertionality_constant, bool distribute_total_amount)"

.PP
computation and assignment of Neumann boundary gradients to target boundary Computes gradients normal to the outer model boundary from influxes (sources) assigned and flagged as NEUMANN elsewhere\&. To do this it needs material parameters from the corresponding flow law, for instance the hydraulic conductivity in the case of Darcy's law\&.

.PP
The convention used is that incoming fluxes have to be positive and outgoing ones negative\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
The method only works for box-shaped models and will only operate on its boundaries\&. Nodal Neumann flagged terms elsewhere will remain untouched\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIboundary\fP is the boundary flag of the box-shaped model, IRREGULAR is valid as well\&.
.br
\fInode_property\fP stores the boundary flux which shall be applied\&.
.br
\fIpropertionality_constant\fP is the element variable the method needs in order to compute the boundary normal gradient which should ensue from the applied flux term, for instance 'hydraulic conductivity' in the case of Darcy's law\&.
.br
\fIdistribute_total_amount\fP tells the method how to interpret the boundary flux term it reads\&. If true, the term will be treated as integrated total for the boundary, else it will be assigned as a flux per unit area\&. 
.RE
.PP

