.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::NodeCenteredFiniteVolumeTransport\fP< dim >::UpdateProjectedVelocitiesAndFluxBalances ()\fR [protected]\fP"
Loops over the finite elements and computes the (costly) projections of the transport velocities onto the facet normals\&. Then it uses these to calculate flux balances for each FV cell which are later used to compensate for divergence terms that may originate in transient flow fields\&.

.PP
Flux balances are calculated only where entire finite volumes can be formed around nodes\&. This is the case for the cells inside a model and based on the concept of halo stencils when the transport region is located inside a mesh (i\&.e\&. the algorithm is restricted to a group)\&.

.PP
The exception are finite volumes at no-flow boundaries which are truncated but for which a flux balance can be obtained because there should not be flux across their boundaries\&.

.PP
For finite volume cells which are cut by the boundary of the \fBRegion\fP no balance is computed\&. Here the value of the flux-balance is set to zero\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The method needs access to the \fBRegion\fP to read the velocity values\&.

.PP
The projected velocities are stored in the private variable 'FV_STENCIL_DATA'\&. The method initializes the FLUX_BALANCE \fBvector<double>\fP that is supplied as second argument\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
The method is called within those methods that compute the Courant number for the current grid\&.

.PP
\fBTodo\fP
.RS 4
fix! - flux balances are not correct for nodes that lie in the inside of the model but on the perimeter of the target region\&.
.RE
.PP

